  "verbalization": "The integrated evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Tolbutamide may interact with Slc15a2, primarily through its role as a sulfonylurea antidiabetic agent. Both Tolbutamide and Glyburide, which are included in the sulfonylurea class, bind to Slc15a2, indicating a shared molecular interaction. This binding is supported by multiple paths, with the lowest common ancestor linking Tolbutamide and Glyburide to the sulfonylurea antidiabetic agent category. The presence of a direct interaction between these compounds and Slc15a2 suggests a possible pharmacological mechanism involving the transporter protein Slc15a2. Additionally, the observed effect of Tolbutamide on Epigastric Fullness, which is mediated by Glyburide, further supports a common pathway involving Slc15a2. However, the exact nature of the interaction and its relevance to Slc15a2 remains to be fully elucidated, requiring further experimental validation.",
